WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.198
Hi, I'm Samantha, co-founder of Caring Companions.

2
00:00:04.198 --> 00:00:07.430
Welcome to the PRN Team! I'm so glad you're here.

3
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.871
First things first: being PRN is not a lesser position.

4
00:00:11.871 --> 00:00:13.210
It never has been.

5
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.878
You're part of our care continuity team.

6
00:00:15.878 --> 00:00:22.890
When a caregiver can't make it, because someone's sick or a car won't start, you help us keep our promise to that family.

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.090
We call it standing in the gap.

8
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:31.193
We have two teams: the PRN Caregiver Team, and the PRN CNA Team.

9
00:00:31.193 --> 00:00:33.620
Both are equally important.

10
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.530
So how does it work?

11
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:42.862
When a shift opens up that fits you, we'll text you the details: the day, the time, and where.

12
00:00:42.862 --> 00:00:44.500
Just reply yes or no.

13
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.728
Saying no is always okay. No guilt, ever.

14
00:00:47.728 --> 00:00:52.500
When you say yes, we'll confirm it, and a family is counting on you.

15
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.981
Your caregiver profile matters, too.

16
00:00:54.981 --> 00:01:01.967
Before you arrive, we share it with the client and their family, so they know who to expect and feel more comfortable.

17
00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:07.710
A short video on your profile is optional, but it can help build trust before you even get there.

18
00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:13.390
Over time, you'll get to know some of our clients, so you're a familiar face when they need someone.

19
00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.294
Tell us the days and times that work for you, and whether short notice is okay.

20
00:01:18.294 --> 00:01:21.810
Every couple of months, we'll check in to keep it up to date.

21
00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:25.294
And between shifts, you're still part of the team.

22
00:01:25.294 --> 00:01:29.870
We'll pass along kind words from families, and we always want your ideas.

23
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.192
Want more hours, or need a break? Just tell us.

24
00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:34.900
We'll always work with you.

25
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.721
What you do matters. Thank you for being part of Caring Companions.

26
00:01:39.721 --> 00:01:42.590
Welcome to the team that stands in the gap!
